While the students' proposed gene panel contains a solid foundation of TCR signaling components (e.g., LCK, ZAP70, ITK, SYK, VAV1, CD3 chains), CBM complex mediators (CARD11, BCL10, MALT1), JAK-STAT pathway members (TYK2, STAT5A/B, STAT6), and key T-cell transcription factors, it exhibits notable omissions and redundancies. Specifically, it omits critical master transcription factors that synergize with NF-κB, AP-1, and T-bet (TBX21) to drive *IFNG* expression—most importantly the **NFAT family** (NFATC1, NFATC2, NFATC3) and additional AP-1/ETS family regulators (JUNB, JUND, FOSB, BATF, ETS1). Additionally, the inclusion of numerous peripheral interleukin and cytokine genes (such as IL31, IL32, IL34, and the IL36 family) at the tail end is less optimal than targeting core intracellular transcription and epigenetic machinery. 

